WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:26.359
Scott Landon doesn’t talk a lot
about his childhood to anybody

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:32.240
and at the same time all his books
and stories draw from that childhood.

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:38.204
He grew up in the home of
a dangerous, abusive parent.

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:45.045
Scott Landon had a very,
very painful, troubled past

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.714
and had to go to Boo’ya Moon to heal.

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:54.137
It’s this sort of unbelievable, epic place.

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:58.308
It’s almost like a physical
landscape of the subconscious.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:02.604
And it’s a place that I use to go and
both draw inspiration and heal myself.

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:06.691
When you play a Scott Landon,

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:10.528
when you play a writer that
is somehow like Stephen King,

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:14.616
you have to carry on that internal
world that a writer has.

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:18.995
Because you always wonder, how is it
when they spend hours and hours

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:22.624
just by themselves in front 
of a computer just creating.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:27.420
They become so internal, so
private and I think Clive has that.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.840
Clive is a brilliant, brilliant actor.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:36.179
You can totally feel and believe that
he has the internal world of a writer.

00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:52.153
Mister Dooley, it’s Lisey Landon.

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.740
You win, I’ll give you
whatever you want.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.784
Meet me here at 10pm.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.453
I won’t call the police, but
please just don’t hurt me.

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:03.039
Don’t hurt me anymore.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.006
That was good.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.717
No, none of this is good.

